# Full existing v2 lifecycle — isolated SQL composition

Owned source: `src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/p5-voice-v2-lifecycle-composition-sql.test.ts` only. This is a focused acceptance suite, with no application source, existing test, SQL, migration, dependency or setting edit. Final test file is formatted and frozen for independent review.

The first focused run passed **22/22 cases**, zero skips, in 8.24 seconds. Initial scoped ESLint passed. No failing fixture/assertion, source correction, constraint change or relaxed deadline was needed. One unused copied type import was removed after the first run; it has no runtime effect. The independent reviewer will execute the final formatted file. Initial logs are `lifecycle-sql-initial.log/json` and `lifecycle-sql-lint-initial.log`.

The fixture now drives the actual `ConversationService` through `createVoiceV2AuthorityIssuer.issue`, then forwards its exact released ciphertext directly in the exact existing five-field admission request to `createVoiceV2CapacityAdmission.admit`, `markCapacity` and retained exact `close`. It uses preserved real AES-GCM/HMAC and actual protected v2 parent/preissue/issuance/current/cleanup/proof/capacity/marker transports, plus existing exact capacity close. There is no manual target seal or issuance registration between stages. Only the fictional staging/approval/quota/pool fixtures are administratively seeded. The actual issuer alone observes the parent, creates/observes the shared generation and registers each immutable issuance.

Coverage comprises:

- Complete service-to-issuer-to-admission-to-marker-to-close path with output HMAC equal to the persisted immutable issuance and v2 Auth-parent binding, separate consumed claim/inspect/marker proofs, and no enabling v1 call. Legacy exact capacity close is deliberately preserved cleanup, not fallback.
- Later fresh bounded authority after prior exact expiry under the same unchanged clear parent and same shared generation. New fingerprint, ciphertext, original issuance time, deadline, attempt and approval are asserted. The full earlier issuance, binding, cleanup, claim, proofs and marked allocation remain unchanged while shared accounting records both debits/occupied slots.
- A fresh genuine issuer authority cannot adopt a prior marked/closed attempt or winner. Retained uncertain marked occupancy blocks later authority when the shared pool is full, without another debit. Further genuine authorities never replenish exhausted cumulative quota.
- Fresh shorter Auth bounds a later authority/claim/proof without changing earlier immutable issuance facts or marked holds.
- Parent revocation and every retained legacy-fence state deny both existing lifecycle revalidation and new issuance; deliberate exact cleanup remains available and does not release marked uncertain holds.
- Returned issuer output supplies no admission after intervening parent, approval, allowlist or Auth-session change. No cleanup, proof, claim or marker writes occur on those denied paths.
- Two concrete final-Auth observation cases: parent revocation or allowlist expiry during the unchanged issuer's twelfth/final Auth await can leave an exact registered token returned as `issued`. The actual downstream admission gate independently rejects it before ownership writes. This records the existing finite snapshot/non-atomic Auth–SQL limitation, not an admission bypass, provider grant or issuer correction.
- Lost/late committed issuance registration and cancelled issuance preserve content-free evidence and do not release a token or launch admission; no automatic retry occurs.
- Exact close before delayed cleanup/marker SQL and after committed delayed marking fences the issuer-fed lifecycle. Late marker acknowledgment cannot reactivate a closed handle; marked operation/slot/held usage remain retained.

The suite executes the preserved SQL chain only in PostgreSQL 18.6/PGlite 0.5.12. Auth, approval, policy, clocks and response-delay/loss hooks are fictional local inputs. Transactions are serialized on one connection; no native multi-session scheduling or HTTP fault-injection acceptance is claimed. Both engine instances close, original SQL clock is restored and Date mocks are restored. All 21 native cases, deployed Auth/current-policy/revocation, host provenance, runtime integration, coordinated quiesced route/privilege cutover and provider/device acceptance remain distinct and unrun.

Exact reproduction:

`BFA_PGLITE_MODULE=/workspace/scratch/205dbad31641/p5-sql-work/environment/node_modules/@electric-sql/pglite/dist/index.js node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run src/lib/ai/conversation/__tests__/p5-voice-v2-lifecycle-composition-sql.test.ts --maxWorkers=2 --testTimeout=15000 --reporter=default --reporter=json --outputFile=../lifecycle-sql-initial.json`

